# Genuine smooth inverse-mode Fourier operators for the original period family

The original selected inverse has a proved common neighborhood with all
real derivative bounds, complex holomorphicity, and exact inverse equations.
On that same neighborhood, its literal product with any rapid coefficient
family has a genuinely smooth Fourier sum. In particular this constructs
the actual inverse-mode operator on every original jointly smooth family,
using its genuine Haar coefficients and no assumed Fourier estimates.
-/
